// cross_mod_out_param — v1.12 param descriptors carry the out flag, so
// an imported `void fill(out int v)` gets an out-marked stub formal.
// Pre-v1.12 the placeholder formal carried no NF_Out and every cross-
// module out-argument call was rejected at compile time; with the flag
// the call binds and the callee's writeback lands in the caller's slot.
void fill(out int v) {
    v = 5;
}
